id:                     E475
trigger_tool: Conan|patch_ng|source
phase: source|conan-create|ci-retry
error_signature: a later conan create re-applies a patch to a source cache left in a postimage state and reports hunk mismatch
severity: 2
category:               conan, source-cache-replay
match_keywords: conan source cache, patch_ng hunk mismatch, repeated create, stale postimage, explicit blank hunk record
title: Reinitialize Conan source trees before ordered patch replay
root_cause: Conan retries can invoke source() against the same recipe cache directory after an earlier run applied patches and failed later; reapplying the ordered patch set then sees postimage bytes instead of the official preimage. Strict patch_ng also requires exact hunk offsets and explicit blank-line records.
affected_scope: Conan recipes that apply ordered patch sets in a reusable source cache, especially when CI retries share a Conan home
verification_cmd: replay the corrected patch with patch_ng 1.19.1 strip=0 fuzz=False on a clean official source; compare the postimage SHA; run GNU patch --dry-run --forward and the outer git diff check; verify a second call cannot change the postimage hash
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: fresh-source-and-exact-hunks
rec_description: Bind every patch to the exact official preimage, use standard blank-line context, and use a new recipe revision or explicit source reset so a retry cannot treat a previous postimage as its preimage; do not rely on patch_ng.apply()'s boolean to detect replay.
rec_command: patch_ng.fromfile(patch).apply(strip=0, root=clean_source_root, fuzz=False); compare postimage SHA256; invoke a second call and assert the postimage hash is unchanged; patch --dry-run --forward -p1; git diff --check
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-closed-cache-rebuild
fallback_description: If source provenance or preimage bytes are uncertain, preserve the failed cache and rebuild from a new source root; do not reverse or reuse a partially patched tree.
fallback_command: retain failed Conan home; create a new recipe revision or isolated source root; replay all patches in declared order
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: retry.*same.*patched.*source|ignore.*hunk.*mismatch|fuzz.*true.*as.*proof
forbid_1_reason: A retry against a postimage can silently skip or misapply an ordered patch and does not prove the official source was transformed correctly.
forbid_1_consequence: Non-reproducible CI results and binaries built from an unproven source state.
forbid_2_pattern: blank.*context.*space|remove.*patch.*because.*cache
forbid_2_reason: A marker-less or whitespace-tainted blank record changes patch grammar or fails the repository whitespace gate.
forbid_2_consequence: Local replay may pass while Conan patch_ng rejects the patch or CI cannot reproduce it.
doc_file: doc/E475.md
last_updated: 2026-08-29
source_event: SDL2 2.32.10 CI 34279 repeated 0016 replay after CI 34238 source failure
source_pr: !7109
